visualcapesaddon.capeRarity.title=Cape Rarity
visualcapesaddon.capeRarity.description=Cape rarities are used to visualize how many people own the cape and how often you can see players wearing it. The Pan Cape is the most common cape you can ever see anytime, while the Bacon Cape is only owned by one player named Miclee because of his idea of a Pigman. (even if it's removed later, it's still the rarest cape of all time)
visualcapesaddon.raritySystem.title=Rarity System
visualcapesaddon.raritySystem.descriptionAbout=This is an extension where cape rarities are actually going to be a rarity in-game where you have less access to the capes that you can choose, but when you get the privilege to equip a 'rare' cape, you can now enjoy and flex it with other players.
visualcapesaddon.raritySystem.descriptionDefaults=The default Rarity System only reduces your access to capes where operators/admins have the ability to give you a cape or a rarity.
visualcapesaddon.raritySystem.description.menu=To open the Capes Menu, get yourself a pumpkin pie and rename it to the anvil as "Cape Selector".  After renaming, you can now start choosing your capes! Cape Selector is still available when the rarity system is turned off.
visualcapesaddon.raritySystem.description.opmenu=To have access to the Operator's Menu, you can use this custom command; both add and remove operators are available.
visualcapesaddon.raritySystem.description.opmenu2=This is how the operator's menu looks; the two methods you can see are already labeled inside the menu.
visualcapesaddon.raritySystem.description.opmenu3=Operators of Cape Menu can deliver any player with any cape or rarity privilege. This is what it should look like when you receive a cape from an operator.


visualcapesaddon.about.description.start=Welcome to Visual Capes Add-on! This add-on allows you to equip one of the capes available that you want, and each player can have their own cape equipped too! There are different cape designs you can choose from, and you can also see its exclusive elytra texture when wearing an elytra.
visualcapesaddon.about.title.features=Features
visualcapesaddon.about.title.getStarted=Get Started
visualcapesaddon.about.description.getStarted=To start your first journey with this add-on, go back and click the 'Start' button, then choose one of the known capes given to the community.
visualcapesaddon.about.description.alreadyStarted=If you are already started, choose a tab shown above.

visualcapesaddon.about.title.equipCape=Equipping a Cape
visualcapesaddon.about.description.equipCape=In this add-on, you can choose what cape you want to equip via commands. It means that if you have access to commands, you can equip or change your cape. You can use either the /event or /function commands.
visualcapesaddon.about.description.equipCape_player=If you are going to apply a cape to another player, you can use either one of these commands:
visualcapesaddon.about.title.capeElytra=Cape with Elytra
visualcapesaddon.about.description.capeElytra=If you equipped one of the capes, you will see that your elytra changed its texture too! (Each cape has its own different elytra texture; some have none; see Capes Tab.)
visualcapesaddon.about.title.removeCape=Removing Cape
visualcapesaddon.about.description.removeCape=If you want to remove your cape, you can use one of these specific /event or /function commands:
visualcapesaddon.about.description.removeCape_player=If you want to remove another player's cape, you can use one of these specific /event or /execute ... function commands:

visualcapesaddon.capesList.description=Here is the list of the Capes you can use. You can see their namespace:name (in-game name for commands use) under their Cape name. (Click the Cape icon to see their Elytra texture, some of them have none, so they use the default texture instead.)

visualcapesaddon.rarity_survival.title=Rarity System with Survival Tweaks
visualcapesaddon.rarity_survival.description1=In this mode, you are able to get unlimited effect duration buffs or activate unique buffs during your survival journey! It allows you to be stronger than before, where you can no longer fear such dangerous situations or battles.
visualcapesaddon.rarity_survival.description2=Note that your active buffs will be gone when you die.
visualcapesaddon.rarity_survival.description3=To get a buff, you need to name any item as "Reward Convert" and have the specific item requirements to register your buffs. Use the "Reward Convert" bottle to open its options. Buffs only activate when you equip a cape that has the same rarity as the buffs you have registered.
visualcapesaddon.rarity_survival.description.register=When you register a buff, it will be displayed in the Capes menu, and you can see what buffs are going to be applied when you equip a cape.
visualcapesaddon.rarity_survival.header.items=Item Tweaks
visualcapesaddon.rarity_survival.description.enchantedapple=Enchanted Golden Apple can now be crafted, but you actually need to have at least two (2) of them to duplicate one (1). The recipe is shown below.
visualcapesaddon.rarity_survival.description.heavycore=Heavy Core can now be obtained in a different way! This is only possible when a player has a buff with an amplifier higher than seven (7). If they die from an explosion, they will drop a Heavy Core, even if they do not have one in their inventory.
visualcapesaddon.rarity_survival.header.customBuffs=Custom Buffs
visualcapesaddon.rarity_survival.description.customBuffs=Custom Buffs, or Unique Buffs, are the buffs that require and consume Heavy Core in your inventory to activate. Most of these buffs cannot be amplified because they are fixed to what they do to the affected entities, players, or yourself. There are currently only five (5) custom buffs available.
visualcapesaddon.rarity_survival.description.cursebinding=All entities within thirty-two (32) blocks will be frozen to their current position, but you will get a permanent darkness effect; both effects only last sixty (60) seconds.
visualcapesaddon.rarity_survival.description.instantrecover1=Instead of using the normal Instant Heal effect, this buff boosts your regeneration and max health for ninety (90) seconds to make it more difficult to get killed.
visualcapesaddon.rarity_survival.description.instantrecover2=Note: This does not prevent you from getting killed by the Self Destruct buff.
visualcapesaddon.rarity_survival.description.netherdomain1=This buff brings every player within sixteen (16) blocks to the nether roof. The casting player sends a ring of fire every seven and a half (7.5) seconds, burning all their victims. If one player dies in the domain, all players from the domain will get teleported back to the overworld's height limit, having a chance to die from fall damage instead.
visualcapesaddon.rarity_survival.description.netherdomain.knownissue=Known Issues
visualcapesaddon.rarity_survival.description.netherdomain2=If no one is a victim of the buff, you need to leave the game and join to automatically escape the domain, but you are not getting teleported back to the overworld.
visualcapesaddon.rarity_survival.description.netherdomain3=When a player leaves the game, even if they are not inside the domain. All players from the domain will be teleported back to the overworld.
visualcapesaddon.rarity_survival.description.selfdestruct=This buff instantly explodes you, dealing seven hundred fifty (750) damage to surrounding players within twenty-five (25) block radius (1500 damage from entities). And players within fifty (50) block radius will be set on fire for thirty (30) minutes if not extinguished.
visualcapesaddon.rarity_survival.description.windpulse=This buff, when active, makes you immune to fall damage and pushes nearby entities upward. Push level is scaled by fall height. Mace cannot stack damage when this buff is active. You can make this buff inactive by sneaking.
visualcapesaddon.rarity_survival.reward.title=Item Requirements Per Rarity


